CHICAGO BIGGER THAN THE BEATLES?  YES!

HOLLYWOOD, CA (DPI) -- A Harvard musicologist has proven that, despite
popular belief to the contrary, the schlock-rock group Chicago *is*
bigger than those hitherto unassailable giants of pop music, The
Beatles.  Interviewed prior to his report being excerpted in Rolling
Stone magazine, Prof. Lorenzo Gastron states his theorem concisely:
"Chicago, they had up to 9 members at some times.  The Beatles consisted
of 4 men, with occasional help on the side from loyal session
musicians.  9 is greater than 4, ipso facto, Chicago is obviously a
bigger group.  I don't see what all the controversy is about."

Protests are planned at several local oldies stations, faced with the
prospect of replacing their Beatles bumper music tapes with "If You
Leave Me Now" and "25 or 6 to 4."  However, says Gastron, the news is
not all bad for Beatles' fans.  "After all, with 4 men, and with God
being essentially 1 being, I have also lent support to the old,
abandoned assertion that The Beatles *were* bigger than God."

Reported by Brian Jones

